1	//! Print spooler watcher thread (M017 T04).
2	//!
3	//! Spawns a dedicated std thread that watches the print spooler for new jobs
4	//! using `FindFirstPrinterChangeNotification`.  When a new job is detected,
5	//! the watcher:
6	//!
7	//! 1. Queries job info via `GetJobW` (level 2).
8	//! 2. If `datatype == "XPS_PASS"`, reads the SPL file and extracts text.
9	//! 3. Classifies content with [`ContentClassifier`].
10	//! 4. Evaluates ABAC policy via [`OfflineManager`].
11	//! 5. Cancels blocked jobs before they reach the printer.
12	//!
13	//! ## Redaction
14	//!
15	//! XPS text content is parsed in-memory and never written to disk or logs.
16	//! Only document name, job ID, and classification tier appear in audit events.
17	
